# Keep Cursor rules in sync

When finishing a **large feature**, **UI/architecture redesign**, **API contract change**, or **layout/convention shift**, update `.cursor/rules/` in the **same PR** before calling the work done.

## Triggers (do this)

- New top-level page sections, providers, or app shell composition
- Renamed/removed canonical files referenced by rules (e.g. deleted `header.tsx`)
- New shared modules agents must use (`profile.ts`, hooks, API helpers)
- Stack upgrades that change defaults (Next major, auth, data layer)
- Chat/streaming or backend contract changes

## Skip (do not churn rules)

- Typos, copy tweaks, one-off bug fixes
- Pure styling polish that does not change structure
- Dep bumps with no behavior/convention change

## Required actions

1. Read existing `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` and fix stale paths, layout, and guardrails
2. Prefer editing the matching rule (`project-overview`, `nextjs-react-ui`, `shared-api-client`, `v2-migration`, `vitest-tests`) over adding overlapping files
3. Keep rules concise and actionable; one concern per file
4. Include the rules diff in the feature PR; check the PR template Cursor-rules item
5. For the full checklist and file map, follow the project skill `.cursor/skills/sync-cursor-rules/SKILL.md`
